---
import Icon from "../shared/Icon.astro";
import SectionLabel from "./SectionLabel.astro";
import LeadBlock from "../shared/LeadBlock.astro";
---

<section id="products" class="home-section container">
  <SectionLabel label="Our products" accent="Open source you can review" />
  <p class="products-intro">
    Our open-source P2P video stack is served{" "}
    <strong>nearly 200 million times a month from jsDelivr alone</strong>. The
    goal behind it: bring the cost of video delivery close to zero, so that
    streaming even 8K video to a large audience is affordable for anyone.
  </p>
  <div class="products-grid">
    <article class="product">
      <div class="product-head">
        <div class="icon-tile">
          <Icon name="share" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>P2P Media Loader</h3>
          <div class="meta">Open source · 1,700+ GitHub stars</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="tagline">
        Cut video delivery costs with peer-to-peer streaming
      </p>
      <p>
        Viewers of the same stream share video segments with each other, so your
        CDN delivers far less —{" "}
        <strong>the bigger the audience, the bigger the savings.</strong> On a
        live stream, 10 viewers can offload up to 90% of traffic and 100 viewers
        up to 99%. HLS and MPEG-DASH, live and on demand, on web, iOS and
        Android — with nothing for viewers to install.
      </p>
      <div class="built">
        <div class="built-label">How we built it</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A set of state-of-the-art algorithms, design and ideas that make P2P
            video delivery not only possible, but almost free for anyone
          </li>
          <li>
            Real-time decisions, segment by segment, on whether to load from
            peers or the CDN — without hurting playback
          </li>
          <li>
            A WebRTC P2P mesh that runs in web browsers and inside native iOS
            and Android apps — no plugins, and free public trackers work out of
            the box
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="links">
        <a class="button primary small" href="/p2p-media-loader/demo">
          Live demo
        </a>
        <a href="/p2p-media-loader/overview">Overview</a>
        <a href="/case-studies/p2p-media-loader">Case study</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/novage/p2p-media-loader">
          <Icon name="github" class="inline-icon" />
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="product">
      <div class="product-head">
        <div class="icon-tile">
          <Icon name="server" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>wt-tracker</h3>
          <div class="meta">Open source · Works with P2P Media Loader</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="tagline">Run your own P2P network on one small server</p>
      <p>
        The server that connects viewers to each other in a P2P Media Loader
        network. Public trackers are fine to start with; for production we
        recommend running your own. It handles{" "}
        <strong>20,000 simultaneous peers</strong> on a VPS with only 2 GiB
        memory and 1 virtual CPU, and self-hosting keeps data about your
        audience on your own infrastructure.
      </p>
      <div class="built">
        <div class="built-label">How we built it</div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            A showcase of getting the most performance out of the Node.js stack,
            with a µWebSockets.js I/O backend and an optimized hot path
          </li>
          <li>
            Eliminates the need for complex horizontal scaling in many P2P video
            projects
          </li>
          <li>
            Robust and well tested: CI, unit tests, static analysis, 100%
            TypeScript
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="links">
        <a class="button primary small" href="/case-studies/wt-tracker">
          Case study
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/novage/wt-tracker">
          <Icon name="github" class="inline-icon" />
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <LeadBlock title="The same team can build your product">
    The engineers behind these projects take on the complete cycle for our
    clients — product design, development, QA, and delivery — for web platforms,
    enterprise systems, and custom software. Bring us a hard problem that needs
    new algorithms, deep performance work, or lower running costs, or a product
    that simply needs to ship on time and keep working. For P2P video, we also
    integrate P2P Media Loader, build custom P2P CDNs, and support them in
    production.
  </LeadBlock>
</section>
